%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e491cf67966164f468c7dd39a46a547f, type: 3}
  m_Name: HowToPlayGuide
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameOfLife::GameOfLife.HowToPlay.HowToPlayGuide
  classicSteps:
  - heading: CELLS AND NEIGHBOURS
    body: 'The board is a grid of cells, and each cell is either alive or empty.
      Every cell has eight neighbours: the cells above, below, to each side and on
      the diagonals. Each generation, every cell counts how many of its neighbours
      are alive, and the whole board changes at once.'
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.6
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - .........
      - .........
      - .........
      - ....OO...
      - ...OO....
      - ....O....
      - .........
      - .........
      - .........
      steps:
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: LONELY CELLS DIE
    body: A living cell with fewer than two living neighbours dies in the next generation.
      A cell on its own, or a pair, never lasts.
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.9
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - .....
        - ...O.
        - .....
        - OO...
        - .....
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: TWO OR THREE NEIGHBOURS KEEP A CELL ALIVE
    body: A living cell with two or three living neighbours survives to the next
      generation. Every cell of this block and this beehive has two or three neighbours,
      so they never change.
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.9
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - .......
      - .......
      - .......
      - .......
      - .......
      - .......
      - .......
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - .......
        - .OO....
        - .OO....
        - .....O.
        - ....O.O
        - ....O.O
        - .....O.
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: CROWDED CELLS DIE
    body: A living cell with more than three living neighbours dies. Here the centre
      cell has four neighbours, so it dies, while the empty corners next to three
      cells fill in.
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.9
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - .....
        - ..O..
        - .OOO.
        - ..O..
        - .....
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: THREE NEIGHBOURS MAKE A NEW CELL
    body: An empty cell with exactly three living neighbours comes alive. Three cells
      in an L fill in the fourth corner, making a block that never changes.
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.9
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - .....
        - .OO..
        - .O...
        - .....
        - .....
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: SHAPES THAT BLINK AND TRAVEL
    body: 'Those four rules are all there is, yet some shapes blink forever, like
      the blinker on the right, and some travel across the board, like the glider.
      The edges of the board are walls: nothing wraps round to the other side.'
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.5
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 0.5
      start:
      - ..........
      - .O........
      - ..O.....O.
      - OOO.....O.
      - ........O.
      - ..........
      - ..........
      - ..........
      steps:
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: PLAYING CLASSIC
    body: 'Tap a cell to bring it to life, and tap it again to remove it. Press PLAY
      to run the generations and again to stop them; you can keep tapping cells and
      dropping patterns while they run. The glider button opens PATTERNS: ready-made
      shapes to drop onto the board, or RANDOM CELLS to scatter cells for you. The
      circular arrow clears the board, and the cog opens Settings, where you can
      change the board size and speed.'
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.6
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - ......
      - ......
      - ......
      - ......
      - ......
      - ......
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - .O....
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ......
        - ..O...
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ......
        - ......
        - O.....
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ......
        - ......
        - .O....
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ......
        - ......
        - ..O...
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: MIXING COLOURS
    body: 'The colour button beside PATTERNS picks the colour of the cells and patterns
      you place: ink, blue, red or yellow. A new cell takes the colour most of its
      three parents share, like the blue cell on the left. If all three parents differ,
      it takes the fourth colour, like the yellow cell on the right.'
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 1
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.8
      start:
      - ...........
      - ...........
      - ...........
      - ...........
      - ...........
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ...........
        - .B.B.......
        - ...........
        - ..R........
        - ...........
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ...........
        - .......O.B.
        - ...........
        - ........R..
        - ...........
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: COLOURS ABSORB EACH OTHER
    body: Cells of one colour that touch, even diagonally, form a cluster. When clusters
      of different colours touch, the bigger one turns the smaller one its own colour,
      straight after every tap, pattern and generation, just as in Versus. Here the
      two blocks are the same size and leave each other alone, until one more red
      cell makes the red cluster bigger.
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 1.4
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.8
      start:
      - ......
      - ......
      - .OORR.
      - .OORR.
      - ......
      - ......
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ......
        - ....R.
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
  versusSteps:
  - heading: YOU AGAINST THE APP
    body: You play blue and the app plays red. Both colours follow the Classic rules,
      and when the timer runs out, whoever has more living squares wins.
    demo:
      versusColours: 1
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.7
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 0.7
      start:
      - .B.....RR.
      - ..B...R..R
      - BBB....RR.
      - ..........
      - ..........
      - .......R..
      - .BB....R..
      - .BB....R..
      steps:
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: 'SETUP: BEAT THE CLOCK'
    body: 'Before the match you and the app place squares at the same time, each
      on your own half of the board: yours is the top half, and the app''s is shaded.
      You both get the same number of setup squares and the same SETUP TIME to place
      them, both set in Settings. Squares still unplaced when the time runs out are
      lost.'
    demo:
      versusColours: 1
      shadeAppHalf: 1
      secondsPerStep: 0.7
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ........
        - .B......
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ......R.
        - ........
        - ........
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ........
        - ........
        - ....B...
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ..R.....
        - ........
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - .....B..
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ....R...
  - heading: DROP A PATTERN
    body: During setup, PATTERNS lets you place a whole shape at once. Every cell
      of it must be empty and on your half, and each cell costs one setup square.
      RANDOM CELLS, at the top of the list, places all your setup squares at once,
      as many as your half has room for, sometimes as whole patterns. The setup clock
      stops while the list is open.
    demo:
      versusColours: 1
      shadeAppHalf: 1
      secondsPerStep: 0.7
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      - ........
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ........
        - .BB.....
        - .BB.....
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ...R....
        - ........
        - ........
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ......R.
        - ........
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - .R......
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ...R....
        - ........
  - heading: STARTING EARLY
    body: Once you have placed at least half of your setup squares, you can press
      PLAY to stop early. Half of your unplaced setup squares are added to your match
      squares, and the app decides whether to save its squares the same way or keep
      placing. The match starts once you are both done or the setup time runs out.
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 0
      start: []
      steps: []
  - heading: THE MATCH
    body: 'After a countdown the generations run against the clock, whose length
      is MATCH TIME in Settings. Each side has the match squares set by MATCH SQUARES,
      plus any it saved by starting early: while the clock runs you can spend yours
      on any empty cell, but the app''s squares must touch a living cell. Press PLAY
      to pause.'
    demo:
      versusColours: 1
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.8
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - ........
      - ........
      - .B......
      - .B......
      - .B......
      - ......R.
      - ......R.
      - ......R.
      steps:
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ..B.....
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
        - ........
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: NEW CELLS TAKE A SIDE
    body: When three cells bring an empty cell to life, it takes the colour that
      most of them share. Here two blue cells outvote one red, so the new cell is
      blue.
    demo:
      versusColours: 1
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.9
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      - .....
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - .....
        - .B.B.
        - .....
        - ..R..
        - .....
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: BIGGER CLUSTERS ABSORB SMALLER ONES
    body: Cells of one colour that touch, even diagonally, form a cluster. When clusters
      of different colours touch, the bigger one turns the smaller one its own colour.
      This happens straight after every placement and every generation, and clusters
      of the same size leave each other alone.
    demo:
      versusColours: 1
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0.9
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 1.5
      start:
      - ......
      - .BB...
      - ......
      - ...RR.
      - ......
      - ......
      steps:
      - kind: 0
        cells:
        - ......
        - ......
        - ...B..
        - ......
        - ......
        - ......
      - kind: 1
        cells: []
  - heading: WINNING
    body: When the timer runs out, the side with more living squares wins, and equal
      counts are a draw. If either side has no squares left on the board, the match
      ends three seconds later, unless that side places one that survives. Press
      PLAY afterwards to start a new match.
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 0
      start: []
      steps: []
  - heading: HOW HARD THE APP PLAYS
    body: Choose EASY, MEDIUM or HARD under OPPONENT in Settings. The harder the
      app, the more of its squares go where they are likely to stay alive.
    demo:
      versusColours: 0
      shadeAppHalf: 0
      secondsPerStep: 0
      secondsBeforeRepeat: 0
      start: []
      steps: []
